    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Isaac Paredes** (70.39) is our clear anchor, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez and an projected bump into the #3 hole. This prime lineup spot, combined with a strong platoon advantage, elevates him well above the rest of the pack. Alongside him, **Brice Turang** (61.75) and **Henry Bolte** (61.38) provide our highest offensive floor. **Brice Turang** remains a critical component of our strategy given the scarcity of stolen bases, and his assumed #1 spot against Kirby offers the volume necessary to hunt those high-value swipes. **Henry Bolte** also profiles as an elite play today, as the matchup against the vulnerable Dobnak allows him to leverage his power-speed profile effectively. **Max Muncy** (60.01) rounds out our top-tier starters, with his score bolstered significantly by the soft 4.70 xERA of the opposing starter.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Vinnie Pasquantino** (51.00) on the bench. He hovered near the lineup threshold, but his output was ultimately throttled by a negative platoon split against the southpaw Jump. While we value **Vinnie Pasquantino**'s floor, the efficiency metrics dictated that we prioritize **Josh Naylor** (56.41) and **Austin Riley** (56.97) despite their own platoon concerns, as they simply offer a higher ceiling in their respective spots. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jose Caballero** (54.79); while his park-adjusted power is enticing, his score is tempered by a steep dynamic platoon penalty and the fact that he is currently projected to bat at the bottom of the order. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with **Jose Caballero** and **Brice Turang**, whose scores depend heavily on their final confirmed batting orders. We have confirmed that **James Wood** and **Tyler Soderstrom** are unavailable due to IL designations, further tightening our depth options. We are counting on **Isaac Paredes** to carry the weight while we wait for more favorable conditions to reintroduce **Vinnie Pasquantino** or **Cole Young** into the mix. We have a solid enough spread of platoon advantages to survive the tougher matchups, but any late lineup shifts pushing **Jose Caballero** or **Brice Turang** out of their assumed slots could force a re-evaluation of our efficiency targets.",
